title: Tooltips
intro: Rest the mouse on anything, a sprite in the world or a button on the HUD, and it says something about itself: in a box by the cursor, or on a line of the HUD.
project: Empty | Tooltips

chapter: A box by the cursor | A Tooltip on a sprite
create: Sprite
rename: Deck
set: Sprite.Size = 2, 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #3A6EA5
add: Tooltip
explain: component:Tooltip | Tooltip | A Tooltip works on anything the mouse can rest on. This deck is just a sprite in the world: no button, no collider.
set: Tooltip.Value = Deck: 3 crates due in 40 seconds
explain: field:Tooltip.Value | Value | What it says. A script sets it to say anything, or, like a Text, it shows an output with Track and Output.
explain: field:Tooltip.Delay | Delay | It shows after the mouse has rested on it this long: half a second, in real time, so it works under a pause menu too.
play
gamehover: Deck
wait: 1
expectvalue: Deck.Tooltip.IsShowing = true
explain: game | By the cursor | The box sits by the cursor, pinned to the screen over everything, and turns to the other side of it near the screen's edge.
gamehover: Deck + 4, 0
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Deck.Tooltip.IsShowing = false
say: Move off, and it goes. Only the topmost tooltip under the mouse shows, and what's on the screen comes before the world.
stop

chapter: On a line of the HUD | Into a named Text
create: Text
rename: Hover Info
set: Text.Value = Hover a deck
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = BottomLeft
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 5, 1
select: Deck
pick: Tooltip.Into = Hover Info
explain: field:Tooltip.Into | Into | Name a Text in Into, and the tooltip writes there instead of the box: an info line on the HUD.
play
gamehover: Deck
wait: 1
expectvalue: Hover Info.Text.Value = Deck: 3 crates due in 40 seconds
explain: game | On the HUD | Rest on the deck, and the line says what the deck's tooltip says.
gamehover: Deck + 4, 0
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Hover Info.Text.Value = Hover a deck
say: Move off, and the line says what it said before.
stop

chapter: On a HUD button | Keys in braces
create: Button
rename: Jump Button
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = TopLeft
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 3, -1.5
add: Tooltip
set: Tooltip.Value = Jumps. Key: {Jump}
explain: field:Tooltip.Value | Value | An action's name in braces shows the key that does it, as in a Text: here, Jump's key. It follows the player's rebinding and the gamepad.
play
gamehover: Jump Button
wait: 1
expectvalue: Jump Button.Tooltip.IsShowing = true
expectvalue: Jump Button.Tooltip.Shown = Jumps. Key: Space
explain: game | On the HUD | A button pinned to the screen shows its tooltip too, with the key filled in.
stop
